---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import { VignetteSelector } from "@components/vignette-selector";

const videos = [
  {
    playbackId: "6X3BeDuvZ2BEgJwaaF9700E9Re1WO02FjkiQKMBU43fR8",
    order: 1,
    description:
      "I shot this in an underground car park during an early morning. The entrance was an inconspicuous doorway that could easily be ignored. It was also completely empty inside, without a single car to be seen or heard, so every sound was audible with a rich reverb throughout the whole space. Most strange of all were the speakers that were continuously playing lounge music. I never expected to find such a fascinating place in a hidden location.",
  },
  {
    playbackId: "UXGlghx6krtNvopFsJd8kRRGdhejPnwavUNNeoOG4mQ",
    order: 2,
    description:
      "While I was exploring Kirchberg I caught a sublte movement in the corner of my eye. As I turned I saw these shoes swinging on the wires of the outdoor light fixtures. This made me realise how many times I walk around without paying attention to the things above me. As a result I decided to capture this moment on film.",
  },
  {
    playbackId: "ETJbmGydT6vsk02eO8uCp49fFLieO5BO5DJVGklS4SlI",
    order: 3,
    description:
      "After spending the day at Katase beach, the sun was setting directly behind Mount Fuji. The alignment looked as if the sun were taking a seat at the top of the mountain. It was difficult to expose for the film, but I believe the final result turrned out quite well. That same evening was also the total lounar eclipse of September 2025. It was a stroke of incredible luck.",
  },
  {
    playbackId: "GH3xlI019KRqjGvfHffUGVJxDJvdaQPw00s9Uhv3JGQ7A",
    order: 4,
    description: "hello world",
  },
  {
    playbackId: "Ziv01nveEVq5PpPW01SK02TmRolIpsaLdZ8FLqXHWYAmp00",
    order: 5,
    description:
      "This video highlights the difficulties of filming on a rangefinder camera. It was shot through a SOM Berthiot Pan Cinor 85, a split image rangefinder. I found out the hard way that the focusing seen through the view was not the focus the camera saw. The result was this footage of passing cars with a heavy bokeh effect. Despite it not being my intention, I still like this footage.",
  },
  {
    playbackId: "2IjjXN1Gd4tGbSzzIZ5Pe01Tzn9I2Azx401PqBxAgh025s",
    order: 6,
    description:
      "I was in Ōgimachi practicing my long exposure night photography when suddenly a thunderstorm put a stop to that. The station was completely empty and I took that as an opportunity to capture the peaceful moment while I waited for the rain to stop or for the next train to arrive. The motion of the rain was not captured as well as I hoped, but I am very happy with the level of detail in the exposure.",
  },
  {
    playbackId: "na96OKmxoqf7GXO7Sx9UFON00ie00gXpcqueRPM3LZhyU",
    order: 7,
    description: "hello world",
  },
  {
    playbackId: "jzJORoDli001swYL1MYFoVkGmlHZhKp01TNnrQKZ01u8oI",
    order: 8,
    description: "",
  },
];
---

<Layout>
  <div class="flex justify-center h-dvh py-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl px-8 w-full flex flex-col">
      <h2 class="text-lg mb-6">vignettes</h2>
      <VignetteSelector videos={videos} client:load />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
